          "Let us slow down and picture the journey the lesson describes. A shopper sees a short video on TikTok, searches Google a few days later and reads reviews, then sees a retargeting ad on Instagram, and finally buys through a link in an email. Four channels touched this one buyer. The question attribution tries to answer is simple: which of those four deserves the credit for the sale? Different models give very different answers, and the answer decides where next month's budget goes. So attribution is not just bookkeeping. It is a vote on which channels live and which ones get switched off.",
