          "Check the logic of the moves. The 75,000 dollars taken from brand search is exactly the 50,000 plus 25,000 given to the two discovery channels. That is why the report shows capital reallocated of 75,000 dollars. It is a shift, not extra spending. Brand search is cut by 37.5 percent of its own budget, since 75,000 divided by 200,000 is 0.375, yet the total spend does not change at all.",
          "Why cut a channel that shows great returns? Because many of those buyers would have found the brand anyway. The lesson says the data-driven view reveals the true incremental impact of discovery, so money moves toward net-new audiences instead of people who were already coming. A mistake is to assume the cut means brand search is bad. It means its last-click credit overstated its causal value.",
