        "example": "An omnichannel fashion group deployed an emergency VBB migration during end-of-season clearance. By uploading BG/NBD + Gamma-Gamma pCLV scores to Google Ads Smart Bidding, the algorithm shifted bids to high-value shoppers seeking premium seasonal collections rather than clearance bargain hunters. The campaign's 30-day realized gross profit increased by $1.8M with zero increase in total media spend.",
        "tryIt": "Simulate an enterprise Value-Based Bidding decile allocator that maps customer pCLV predictions into dynamic ad auction bid multipliers.",
        "code": "class ValueDecileBidAllocator:\n    def __init__(self, base_cpc: float = 3.00):\n        self.base_cpc = base_cpc\n\n    def allocate_bids_by_p_clv(self, customer_profiles: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:\n        # Sort customers by predicted 1yr pCLV descending\n        sorted_custs = sorted(customer_profiles, key=lambda x: x[\"predicted_1yr_pclv\"], reverse=True)\n        n = len(sorted_custs)\n        \n        results = []\n        for rank, c in enumerate(sorted_custs):\n            percentile = (rank / n) * 100.0\n            \n            # Decile assignment (1 to 10)\n            decile = int(percentile // 10) + 1\n            if decile > 10:\n                decile = 10\n                \n            # Dynamic multiplier curve: Decile 1 gets 3.5x, Decile 10 gets 0.25x\n            if decile == 1:\n                multiplier = 3.5\n                strategy = \"AGGRESSIVE_EXPANSION\"\n            elif decile <= 3:\n                multiplier = 2.0\n                strategy = \"CORE_GROWTH\"\n            elif decile <= 7:\n                multiplier = 1.0\n                strategy = \"MAINTAIN_STANDARD\"\n            else:\n                multiplier = 0.25\n                strategy = \"SUPPRESS_BID\"\n\n            cpc_bid = round(self.base_cpc * multiplier, 2)\n            results.append({\n                \"customer_id\": c[\"customer_id\"],\n                \"predicted_pclv\": c[\"predicted_1yr_pclv\"],\n                \"decile\": decile,\n                \"strategy\": strategy,\n                \"bid_multiplier\": multiplier,\n                \"final_cpc_bid\": cpc_bid\n            })\n            \n        return results\n\nallocator = ValueDecileBidAllocator(base_cpc=3.00)\n\nsample_cohort = [\n    {\"customer_id\": \"C-101\", \"predicted_1yr_pclv\": 1450.0},\n    {\"customer_id\": \"C-102\", \"predicted_1yr_pclv\": 820.0},\n    {\"customer_id\": \"C-103\", \"predicted_1yr_pclv\": 310.0},\n    {\"customer_id\": \"C-104\", \"predicted_1yr_pclv\": 120.0},\n    {\"customer_id\": \"C-105\", \"predicted_1yr_pclv\": 35.0}\n]\n\nallocated = allocator.allocate_bids_by_p_clv(sample_cohort)\nfor c in allocated:\n    print(f\"Customer {c['customer_id']} (pCLV: ${c['predicted_pclv']}) -> Decile {c['decile']}, Multiplier: {c['bid_multiplier']}x, Bid: ${c['final_cpc_bid']} [{c['strategy']}]\")\n",
        "output": "Customer C-101 (pCLV: $1450.0) -> Decile 1, Multiplier: 3.5x, Bid: $10.5 [AGGRESSIVE_EXPANSION]\nCustomer C-102 (pCLV: $820.0) -> Decile 3, Multiplier: 2.0x, Bid: $6.0 [CORE_GROWTH]\nCustomer C-103 (pCLV: $310.0) -> Decile 5, Multiplier: 1.0x, Bid: $3.0 [MAINTAIN_STANDARD]\nCustomer C-104 (pCLV: $120.0) -> Decile 7, Multiplier: 1.0x, Bid: $3.0 [MAINTAIN_STANDARD]\nCustomer C-105 (pCLV: $35.0) -> Decile 9, Multiplier: 0.25x, Bid: $0.75 [SUPPRESS_BID]",
        "check": {
          "question": "How does segmenting customer populations by predicted 1-year pCLV deciles empower automated ad bidding systems?",
          "options": [
            "It lets bidding algorithms bid the same amount for every decile, so that spend is spread evenly and the learning phase completes faster.",
            "It lets bidding algorithms bid more on bottom-decile prospects, since low-value cohorts have the largest room for growth in future revenue.",
            "It allows bidding algorithms to place aggressive bids on top-decile prospects while drastically suppressing bids on low-value cohorts, maximizing portfolio ROI.",
            "It lets bidding algorithms switch off all prospecting, since decile data shows which existing customers should be retargeted instead."
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "answerIndex": 2,
          "why": "pCLV decile segmentation enables algorithmic bidding engines to bid aggressively (up to 3.5x or higher) to acquire prospective customers resembling top-decile VIPs while suppressing bids on lower deciles prone to high churn and negative margins.",
          "explanation": "pCLV decile segmentation enables algorithmic bidding engines to bid aggressively (up to 3.5x or higher) to acquire prospective customers resembling top-decile VIPs while suppressing bids on lower deciles prone to high churn and negative margins."
        }
