      "Part 1 (Lexical Search Limitations & The Semantic Gap: Vocabulary Mismatch & Polysemy): The vocabulary mismatch problem arises because human language offers multiple synonymous expressions for the same concept; lexical matching fails when query terms do not literally appear in the document.",
      "Part 2 (Dense Retrieval & Representation Learning: Bi-Encoders, Cross-Encoders & Sentence Transformers): Bi-encoders separate query and document encoding, enabling offline vector pre-computation and fast ANN search; cross-encoders jointly encode query and document, providing higher accuracy but prohibitive computational cost at scale.",
