          "The architecture of our Capstone Control Tower comprises four integrated processing engines: Engine 1 is the Query Understanding & Intent Classifier, normalizing noisy user strings, correcting spelling via noisy-channel language models, and categorizing intent into Informational, Commercial, Transactional, or Navigational archetypes. Engine 2 is the Dual-Retriever Hybrid Search Engine, querying inverted indices and dense vector spaces concurrently and synthesizing candidate lists via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF $k=60$). Engine 3 is the Passage-Level MaxP Extractor, segmenting long-form documents into semantic windows to eliminate length dilution and surface exact answer snippets. Engine 4 is the Search Console BigQuery Analytics & Cannibalization Control Tower, modeling log-logistic CTR decay curves, detecting URL splitting conflicts, and projecting commercial ROI.",
